{
  "id": "lateral-inhibition",
  "term": "lateral inhibition",
  "definition": "Lateral inhibition is a visual-system coding process in which interneurons collect input from neighboring cells and send inhibitory feedback to them. In the retina, this creates center-surround receptive fields that sharpen spatial contrast and help explain how nearby areas can change perceived brightness.",
